/-!
# Extracting effective kernel twists from split-torus torsor sections

Source: Stacks Project, groupoids.tex, Tags 0EKK and 0EKL, and descent.tex,
proposition-fpqc-descent-quasi-coherent. The section consequence uses the frame-product
Laurent decomposition in constructions.tex, Tags 01M2 and 01LX.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-split-torus-torsor-section-extraction).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped CategoryTheory.MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A nonzero section upstairs yields a nonzero section of an invertible kernel twist.
Source: Stacks Project, Tags 0EKK and 0EKL, iterated and descended via
proposition-fpqc-descent-quasi-coherent in descent.tex; constructions.tex, 01M2 and 01LX.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-split-torus-torsor-section-extraction).

Proof:
1. Apply lem-sfb-split-torus-torsor-frame-geometry to identify the torsor with the
   simultaneous frames of invertible modules A_i, for i in Fin r. For r = 0 this
   identifies the torsor map with the identity of the base.
2. For n in Z^r, put N_n = tensor_i A_i^(-n_i). The normalized isomorphism in
   lem-sfb-frame-product-laurent-algebra identifies the direct sum of the N_n with
   q_* O_P. On a chart with frames e_i it sends tensor_i e_i^(-n_i) to z^n, where
   the universal frame is z_i q^*e_i; this fixes the sign of the character.
3. Send l tensor a in L tensor N_n to the product of q^*l and the n-th Laurent
   coefficient image of a. The tensor and pullback constructions make this a sheaf
   map from the direct sum of L tensor N_n to q_* q^*L. On a chart generated by l
   it is precisely the Laurent algebra isomorphism. The local inverses agree
   since they invert the same map, so the sheaf map is an isomorphism.
4. Transport a nonzero section upstairs through this inverse. The projections to
   the character summands detect zero: locally a section of the sheafified direct
   sum comes from finitely many summands, and vanishing of every coefficient
   makes that local finite sum zero. Sheaf uniqueness then makes the whole section
   zero. Thus some component is nonzero; commuting global sections with arbitrary
   coproducts is unnecessary.
5. Take N to be its N_n. The tensor of the powers of local generators shows it is
   invertible. The corresponding powers of the global universal frames, using
   dual frames for negative powers, give O_P isomorphic to q^*N by evaluation.
   The chosen coefficient is the required nonzero section of L tensor N. In rank
   zero take N = O_X. No group structure on the base or total space is used. -/
theorem split_torus_torsor_section_extraction
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (X : Over (Spec (.of k))) (P : Over X.left)
    [CompactSpace X.left] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X.left]
    [Flat P.hom] [Surjective P.hom] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation P.hom]
    [QuasiCompact P.hom] [QuasiSeparated P.hom] (r : ℕ)
    (act : Over.mk (P.hom ≫ X.hom) ⊗ (MultiplicativeType.splitTorus k r).X ⟶
      Over.mk (P.hom ≫ X.hom))
    (hone : ∀ (U : Over (Spec (.of k))) (p : U ⟶ Over.mk (P.hom ≫ X.hom)),
      lift p (1 : U ⟶ (MultiplicativeType.splitTorus k r).X) ≫ act = p)
    (hmul : ∀ (U : Over (Spec (.of k))) (p : U ⟶ Over.mk (P.hom ≫ X.hom))
      (t t' : U ⟶ (MultiplicativeType.splitTorus k r).X),
      lift (lift p t ≫ act) t' ≫ act = lift p (t * t') ≫ act)
    (hinvariant : act.left ≫ P.hom =
      (fst (Over.mk (P.hom ≫ X.hom)) (MultiplicativeType.splitTorus k r).X).left ≫
        P.hom)
    (torsor : ∃ e :
      (Over.mk (P.hom ≫ X.hom) ⊗ (MultiplicativeType.splitTorus k r).X).left ≅
        pullback P.hom P.hom,
      e.hom ≫ pullback.fst _ _ =
        (fst (Over.mk (P.hom ≫ X.hom)) (MultiplicativeType.splitTorus k r).X).left ∧
      e.hom ≫ pullback.snd _ _ = act.left)
    (L : X.left.Modules) [L.IsInvertible]
    (hsection : ∃ s : Γ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback P.hom).obj L, ⊤), s ≠ 0) :
    ∃ N : X.left.Modules, N.IsInvertible ∧
      Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback P.hom).obj N ≅ 𝟙_ P.left.Modules) ∧
      ∃ s : Γ(L ⊗ N, ⊤), s ≠ 0 := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
